                <pb facs="0806" n="694" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg694"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Lyon to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-01-28"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 28, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 222.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    Liberian Legislature in joint session yesterday authorized the appointment of a
                    commission to visit the United States of America. The commission will leave as
                    early as possible after the adjournment of the legislature in February. The
                    appointment of the commission may be regarded as the popular expression of the
                    people.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ernest Lyon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
